{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Fetch me.</b> They are mine and are not stolen, for so Yitzchak wrote her in her ketubah — to take two kids of the goats every day (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Two kids of the goats.</b> Were two kids of the goats Yitzchak's meal? Rather, one he offered as his Paschal offering and one he made into delicacies — in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer." "<b>Such as I love.</b> For the taste of the kid is like the taste of the deer."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:44.742432680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}